(5817481, 845922, 45672, '<td valign="top">What a great shot!  Congrats on the ribbon.  You have a very impressive portfolio here on DPC.  I enjoyed browsing through all your photos.</td>', 'What a great shot!  Congrats on the ribbon.  You have a very impressive portfolio here on DPC.  I enjoyed browsing through all your photos.', '2010-01-18 22:58:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(5817546, 845922, 38930, '<td valign="top">Wow, thanks for all the nice comments! Finally won a blue!! :)<br/> <br/>As for those who voted low and thought this photo didn''t fit the challenge, the boat was shipwrecked and later destroyed. Here''s the story: <br/>The captain apparently purchased this shrimp boat one month ago and was new to the layout of this harbor, so at 2 in the morning he missed the entrance and the boat started getting pounded by the huge waves. The 5 crew members had to be rescued by the Coast Guard, and the 40'' boat ended up where you see it here. By morning the waves had started breaking pieces off the boat, and a backhoe tried in vain to bring it to shore. (you can sorta see the rope where they are trying to pull it) The rope was a bad idea, and you can see where it has started to break a hole in the hull. The next day they had gotten nowhere, so they destroyed the boat and hauled it away in dump trucks. All the shrimp were later set free.<br/> <br/>So for those who thought this didn''t fit the challenge, it''d be nice to have the benefit of the doubt, and instead vote on the picture for its technical qualities. This is a fun site, and we''re not all out to cheat and lie our way through challenges. :)</td>', 'Wow, thanks for all the nice comments! Finally won a blue!! :) As for those who voted low and thought this photo didn''t fit the challenge, the boat was shipwrecked and later destroyed. Here''s the story: The captain apparently purchased this shrimp boat one month ago and was new to the layout of this harbor, so at 2 in the morning he missed the entrance and the boat started getting pounded by the huge waves. The 5 crew members had to be rescued by the Coast Guard, and the 40'' boat ended up where you see it here. By morning the waves had started breaking pieces off the boat, and a backhoe tried in vain to bring it to shore. (you can sorta see the rope where they are trying to pull it) The rope was a bad idea, and you can see where it has started to break a hole in the hull. The next day they had gotten nowhere, so they destroyed the boat and hauled it away in dump trucks. All the shrimp were later set free. So for those who thought this didn''t fit the challenge, it''d be nice to have the benefit of the doubt, and instead vote on the picture for its technical qualities. This is a fun site, and we''re not all out to cheat and lie our way through challenges. :)', '2010-01-19 00:43:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(5817579, 846049, 86218, '<td valign="top">When I saw this pic....I knew it would do well. It captured my heart. kids dont play any more in the modern world..They collect dust behind computers and electronic games. They have become adults...Never content with what they have always looking at what they dont have or still want. Kids dont look at the obstacles. They create opportunities. Im so glad you could have fun with them.</td>', 'When I saw this pic....I knew it would do well. It captured my heart. kids dont play any more in the modern world..They collect dust behind computers and electronic games. They have become adults...Never content with what they have always looking at what they dont have or still want. Kids dont look at the obstacles. They create opportunities. Im so glad you could have fun with them.', '2010-01-19 01:59:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(5817776, 846053, 36141, '<td valign="top">Sorry, forgot to finish that line. I was going to say that I probably would like the original better, too much editing for my taste. And seeing the original now, I thought it right, I like the original better.</td>', 'Sorry, forgot to finish that line. I was going to say that I probably would like the original better, too much editing for my taste. And seeing the original now, I thought it right, I like the original better.', '2010-01-19 07:45:14.000000', NULL, 0),
